Student Recruitment Quick Guide

Bachelor of Computer Science + Master of Data Science

Proposed four-year online double degree | Internal advisor guide

30-second course pitch
A flexible online pathway for students who want broad computer science capability and advanced data science skills. Students can graduate with two qualifications in four years, explore emerging technologies beyond AI and learn through industry-informed content—without needing to relocate or meet a high ATAR threshold.

Course at a glance

Course information

Details

Award

Bachelor of Computer Science and Master of Data Science

Duration

Four years: three years focused on computer science and one year focused on data science

Delivery

Online, designed for students who cannot attend regular face-to-face classes

Entry

ATAR 75; no advanced mathematics prerequisite, with assumed knowledge only

Study focus

Computer science, artificial intelligence, data science, cybersecurity, digital trust, digital twins and quantum computing

Related pathway

A three-year standalone Bachelor of Computer Science is also proposed

Best-fit students

Recent Year 12 graduates or early-career students who want a future-facing technology degree.

Students outside easy reach of a campus who still want a structured university pathway.

Working adults seeking a career change or progression into higher-value technology roles.

Learners attracted to both computing foundations and advanced data capability.

Lead with these benefits

Two recognised qualifications completed in four years.

Online access and an ATAR 75 entry point broaden the pathway into technology.

Emerging technology coverage extends beyond AI to digital twins, quantum computing and digital trust.

Proposed curriculum input and learning content from AWS, Cisco, Microsoft and Palo Alto. Confirm exact commitments before advising.

Questions to guide the conversation

Interest: What interests you more: building technology, working with data, or combining both?

Goal: Are you looking to enter technology, change careers or progress in your current field?

Study fit: Would online study help you balance work, caring responsibilities or location?

Confidence: How do you feel about mathematics and returning to structured study?

Address common concerns

Mathematics: No advanced mathematics prerequisite is proposed; explain that assumed knowledge still applies.

Online support: Highlight webinars, one-to-one consultations and proposed AI-enabled support.

Career value: Connect the combined qualification to broad foundational and advanced skills. Avoid promising a specific role or salary.

Time: Talk through the four-year commitment and confirm the study load once approved.

Confirm before advising

The following details are still subject to university confirmation:

Fees and CSP availability

Intake dates

Study load and final course map

Alternative entry pathways and credit or recognition of prior learning

Internships, scholarships and certifications

Accreditation and approved career outcomes

Exact industry partner commitments

Important: Do not use the claim “only course of its kind in NSW” until it has been approved and substantiated.
